---
.title = "Get Secure Random Bytes through Io",
.date = "2026-09-29",
.author = "ZigCC",
.layout = "section.shtml",
---

Operations that need randomness receive the same `std.Io` context. `std.Io.randomSecure` uses the
context's secure random source and fills a caller-owned buffer. The existing Network recipes
demonstrate the related `std.Io.net` interfaces for TCP, UDP, DNS, and HTTP operations.

